Advertise and accept reset_stream_at under draft -11's codepoint as well.

Applies to picoquic 7e77d01d9ec4fd03f71529637549863917aeb793, after 0001 to
0010; it also applies on its own.

picoquic sends and reads the reset_stream_at transport parameter only under
draft-ietf-quic-reliable-stream-reset-07's 0x17f7586d2cb571. Drafts -10 and
-11 assign it 29 (0x1d); the RESET_STREAM_AT frame (0x24) is unchanged. A
peer that knows only 29 -- quicly, neqo, xquic, moq-quic -- and picoquic each
ignore the other's parameter, so neither enables the extension, and
WebTransport over HTTP/3 draft-16, which requires it from both endpoints,
refuses the session (seen against h2o in MoQ interop, 2026-10-17).

picoquic_tp_reset_stream_at_v11 (0x1d) is added and picoquic_tp_reset_stream_at
keeps its value, so existing callers are unchanged. When the extension is
enabled both codepoints are sent, each empty, as quic-go, kwik and aiopquic
do, until peers that know only draft-07 (google/quiche, mvfst) move to 29.
Either one received enables the extension; a value on either one is
TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR, whether or not the other is valid. QMux shares the
encoder and decoder. Session tickets do not store this parameter (tp_0rtt),
so nothing remembered is tied to one codepoint. picoquic_set_tp_value_by_type,
the names and the qlog writers accept both.
Based on gmarzot/aiopquic patches/picoquic-reset-stream-at-tp.patch (v0.6.1).
Tests: picoquictest transport_param (each codepoint alone, both in each
order, a value on 29 alone and beside an empty draft-07), transport_param_log
and transport_param_default.

Upstream picoquic master still defines only the draft-07 codepoint as of
2026-10-21:
